# heimdall-ui unit — shipped by IaC (apps/log-anomaly). Stub.
# [Unit]/[Service] to be filled at Phase 2c/3.
#
# The operator console. Bind it to loopback and put the cluster's existing TLS
# terminator + OIDC in front; do NOT expose it directly.
#
#   REQUIRED
#     HEIMDALL_UI_AUTH           oidc | token | none. NO DEFAULT — it must be chosen.
#                                Defaulting to `none` would let a forgotten variable
#                                publish the console; defaulting to anything else would
#                                make a LAN dashboard fail mysteriously.
#     HEIMDALL_UI_OPERATORS      comma-separated operator ids allowed to WRITE (required
#                                except in `none` mode). Naming nobody is legal and makes
#                                the console read-only — but it must be explicit, so a
#                                forgotten var can never silently grant write access.
#     HEIMDALL_ENGINE_STATE_DB   engine state.db — finding ledger + suppressions
#     HEIMDALL_BRIDGE_DB         bridge db — notify_outbox + notify_delivery
#     HEIMDALL_TEXTFILE_DIR      where the heartbeat .prom files are written
#
#   MODE: token — a shared bearer token, for automation or for fronting the console
#   with something that already authenticates.
#     HEIMDALL_UI_TOKEN          >= 24 chars, required on EVERY route including reads.
#                                Via LoadCredential, never inline.
#
#   MODE: oidc — humans log in against Pocket-ID / Keycloak / any OIDC provider.
#   Discovery runs at BOOT, so a bad issuer stops the daemon rather than surfacing
#   as a broken login later. Operators are matched against sub, email, OR
#   preferred_username, since providers differ in which they populate.
#     HEIMDALL_UI_OIDC_ISSUER          e.g. https://id.example/  (discovery base)
#     HEIMDALL_UI_OIDC_CLIENT_ID
#     HEIMDALL_UI_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET   optional for a public client
#     HEIMDALL_UI_OIDC_REDIRECT_URL    must equal the registered callback, ending /callback
#     HEIMDALL_UI_SESSION_KEY          >= 24 chars; HMAC key signing the session cookie
#     HEIMDALL_UI_INSECURE_COOKIES     opt OUT of Secure cookies for a plain-HTTP LAN
#                                      deployment. Off by default — a session cookie
#                                      sent over HTTP is a session cookie on the wire.
#
#   MODE: none — a LAN dashboard, no login at all. READ-ONLY by default.
#     HEIMDALL_UI_ANONYMOUS_WRITES  allow writes with no identity. Off by default,
#                                   because a mute with no actor leaves the suppression
#                                   ledger with nobody to attribute it to. When on, the
#                                   ledger records the actor as plainly unauthenticated.
#
#   OPTIONAL
#     HEIMDALL_UI_LISTEN               default 127.0.0.1:9095
#     HEIMDALL_SUPPRESSIONS_FILE       declarative suppressions.json
#     HEIMDALL_SINKS_FILE              the SAME file the notifier reads, so the delivery
#                                      view cannot disagree with what is actually drained
#     HEIMDALL_DIGEST_DIR              the Tier-2 digest (<dir>/latest.json). Unset means
#                                      the digest page says so rather than showing nothing.
#     HEIMDALL_ANALYST_RUN_DIR         the Tier-3 persisted runs (<dir>/<run_id>.json).
#                                      Same directory the analyst writes; the console only
#                                      reads it.
#     HEIMDALL_SPOOL_DIR               the detector's per-finding redacted evidence docs.
#                                      Unset means the detail page says evidence is
#                                      unavailable rather than showing an empty box.
#     HEIMDALL_UI_BRIDGE_HEALTHZ_URL   the bridge renders no heartbeat textfile; without
#                                      this it is reported ABSENT rather than healthy
#
#   OPERATOR ACTIONS — opt-in, per action, as a FIXED argv. Nothing from an HTTP
#   request ever reaches these command lines and no shell is involved. Unset means
#   the action does not exist: the endpoint answers 501 and no button is rendered.
#     HEIMDALL_UI_ACTION_RERUN_DETECT   e.g. /bin/systemctl start heimdall-detect.service
#     HEIMDALL_UI_ACTION_FORCE_DRAIN    e.g. /bin/systemctl start heimdall-drain.service
#     HEIMDALL_UI_ACTION_<NAME>_TIMEOUT_SECONDS   optional, default 30
#
# The child of an action runs with an EMPTY environment and in its own process
# group, which is killed on timeout — a `systemctl` that hands off to systemd
# cannot outlive the deadline. Granting this unit the right to start those units
# is a PolicyKit/sudoers decision made outside this file; if you do not grant it,
# leave the action vars unset rather than running the console as root.
